The lab
The lab environment demonstrates a complete Python-based BMP pipeline executing unprivileged over loopback TCP (127.0.0.1). It consists of four modular source components:

bmp/bmp.py: A pure-Python codec defining binary pack/unpack logic for BMP v3 Common Headers, Per-Peer Headers, Initiation, Peer Up, Peer Down, Route Monitoring, and Statistics frames, along with a minimal BGP UPDATE/OPEN parser.
bmp/routersim.py: A simulated router (AS 64500) that manages two eBGP peers (isp-a IPv4, isp-b IPv6), enforces an inbound security policy filtering bogons (100.64.0.0/10, 198.18.0.0/15, /25 prefixes), sets LOCAL_PREF, and streams structured BMP frames.
bmp/station.py: A stream-framing BMP collector that accumulates bytes from socket buffers, parses complete BMP frames using length headers, and maintains per-peer pre-policy and post-policy state tables.
bmp/lab.py: The test harness that executes five distinct analytical scenarios: chunked TCP transport, inbound policy drop evaluation, raw Per-Peer Header inspection, framing failure demonstration, and post-policy visibility limitations.

A simplification to know about. In routersim.py, for implementation brevity without introducing third-party dependencies, isp-b is defined with an IPv6 peer address (2001:db8:b::1), but NLRI entries are emitted with standard IPv4 prefixes and unicast NEXT_HOP attributes. Production implementations carrying IPv6 routes utilize MP_REACH_NLRI (RFC 4760).


